<p>Use this dialog box to set a user ID, file name, password and user name 
 for the print job.</p>
<p>This dialog box is accessible by clicking <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 after selecting <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Setup</span> menu or on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab.</p>
<p>Depending on the Job Type you selected, the setting items may vary.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="userid" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">User ID:</span></p>
<p>Select whether to create your own user ID or to use your Windows login 
 name as your user ID. This ID is used to specify the file to be printed 
 or deleted from the printer's control panel. It also identifies individual 
 users in the job history.</p>
<p>The user ID is required for all types of job except <span class="Term-Soft">Normal 
 Print</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> jobs.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Create Own ID</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Specify a user ID of your choice in the <span class="Term-Soft">Enter 
 User ID:</span> box.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Windows Login Name</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Auto-specifies your Windows login name as your user 
 ID.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">If the number 
 of characters in your Windows login name exceeds 20 single-byte characters, 
 your user ID will only display up to 20 single-byte characters.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="enter" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Enter User ID:</span></p>
<p>Enter the user ID using up to eight characters, which are alphanumeric 
 (a-z, A-Z, and 0-9) characters and symbols ('_', '.', '-', '/', and ':'). 
 </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="filename" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">File Name:</span></p>
<p>You can optionally set a file name for each file depending on your purpose.</p>
<p>Enter a file name using up to 16 single-byte or 8 double-byte characters 
 except double quotation mark.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you selected 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Hold Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Stored 
 Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Stored Print (Shared)</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Store and Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Store and 
 Print (Shared)</span>, or <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="password" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Password:</span></p>
<p>Enter a password using 4 to 8 digits when you selected <span class="Term-Soft">Locked 
 Print</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> list.</p>
<p>You can also enter a password optionally if you selected <span class="Term-Soft">Stored 
 Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Stored Print (Shared)</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Store and Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Store and 
 Print (Shared)</span>, or <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> list.</p>
<p>When <span class="Term-Soft">Locked Print</span>, <span class="Term-Soft">Stored Print</span>, or <span class="Term-Soft">Stored Print (Shared)</span> is selected and the encryption function is enabled, the input range is from 4 to 32 alphanumeric (a-z, A-Z, and 0-9) characters.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="username" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">User Name:</span></p>
<p>Enter a user name using up to 16 single-byte or 8 double-byte characters 
 except double quotation marks. This is used to indicate to whom the file 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> belongs.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="time" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Set Print Time</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print a job at a specified time.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you selected 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Hold Print</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Type:</span> list. Depending on the printer you are using, this function 
 may not be available.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="fnumber" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Folder Number:</span></p>
<p>Enter a number for the folder where you want to store the document, 
 using a value between 0 and 200.</p>
<p>If you specify "0", the document will be stored in the <span class="Term-Hard">Shared Folder</span>.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you selected 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Type:</span> list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="fpass" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Folder Password:</span></p>
<p>If the folder is password-protected, enter the password.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if you selected 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Document Server</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job 
 Type:</span> list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the entries and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
